# Both images build from the repository root, so this list is what keeps a
# multi-hundred-megabyte build context from being sent to the daemon — and, more
# importantly, what keeps a local .env out of an image.

.git
.github

# ---- secrets: never in an image, regardless of .gitignore ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
service-account*.json
credentials*.json

# ---- Python ----
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# ---- Node ----
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*

# ---- Large artefacts nothing in a running container reads ----
docs/screenshots
# The backend image does not copy the harness at all. The frontend image copies
# only evals/reports/latest.json, which its prebuild step prefers over the
# committed copy so the deployed /evaluation page belongs to the deployed commit.
# Everything else under evals/reports/ is a dated artefact no build needs.
evals/reports/*.json
!evals/reports/latest.json
